 "seed": 13,
 "notes": "1921 three-storey flats in cream smooth stucco, no bays. Two wide flat picture windows per upper storey with a relief panel group under each top window, a thin flat parapet cap, and at street level two cream panelled garage doors in arched recesses with a small glazed entry door beside the right one. Adds the narrow centre slot window on each upper storey (a thin ribbon span). Dark bronze window sash with a horizontal transom bar; relief panels under the top windows now read as framed panels (raised frame bars, a centre garland group flanked by two rosette squares) and sit just under the top windows; two small bracket knobs under a deeper parapet cap; the garage infills are cream panelled doors (a panel grid on a cream leaf) rather than roll-up slats; the entry door is door height inside the right-hand recess beside the garage. Round-arched heads and the storey-2 railing have no style key. Shorter garage storey (floorsM 3.3 / 3.45) so the blank band between the garage heads and the first window storey shrinks; relief panels and parapet knobs moved down with the storeys; warmer cream wall; the garage openings run to 2.9 m with a shadowed recess head band over beige doors of four rows of horizontal panels and a small dark vent grille, the glazed entry door beside the right garage in the same recess; dark window frames with a transom bar across the top band of every upper window. Round-arched heads still have no style key. Applied: round-arched garage heads (hbArchDoors, semicircle approximates the segmental arch), flat header band removed, 4x5 raised-panel grid, slightly warmer cream. Not expressible: Juliet railing, narrow-wide-narrow casement split, round medallions. Door-mirror claim SKIPPED. Applied: arch ring tinted as the wall so the smooth basket arches lose the stone-surround look, garage panel lines darkened to read as raised panels. 3-light windows have no key (mullion already reads). Applied: warm cream ece3cf; removed the round arch/voussoir surrounds; garage openings now rectangular with slightly rounded (basket) upper corners. Medallion frieze already sits only under the storey-2 windows (no duplicate in the style). Tint lift (2026-10-02): wall tints lifted toward the sunlit paint (t' = 1-(1-t)k).",
